msgid "A ceiling, not a promise: it assumes a control that works every time, which none does, so it ranks what is worth treating rather than announcing a gain. Techniques overlap, so the amounts do not add up across techniques."
msgstr "A ceiling, not a promise: it assumes a control that works every time, which none does, so it ranks what is worth treating rather than announcing a gain. Techniques overlap, so the amounts do not add up across techniques."

msgid "A claim from a producer is read only when the source confidence it carries reaches this level. Claims below it are stored, not read: nothing is discarded, and lowering the gate brings them back without re-importing anything. The attack outcome probabilities OpenCRQ's internal model gives each threat do not depend on this gate. A new level applies the next time a list is read."
msgstr "A claim from a producer is read only when the source confidence it carries reaches this level. Claims below it are stored, not read: nothing is discarded, and lowering the gate brings them back without re-importing anything. The attack outcome probabilities OpenCRQ's internal model gives each threat do not depend on this gate. A new level applies the next time a list is read."

